.TH VJPEG 1 "Aug 21, 2026"
.SH NAME
vjpeg \- visual tool to experience the compression parameters available in sjpeg
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vjpeg
.RI [ options ] " input_file " [ input_file2 " ...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents the
.B vjpeg
command.
.PP
\fBvjpeg\fP compresses a PNG, JPEG or PPM image, or recompresses a JPEG image,
using an interactive OpenGL-based viewer to visually compare the source
picture against the effect of sjpeg's compression parameters, adjusted live.
.PP
Several input files can be supplied; use the
.B +
and
.B \-
keys (see KEYS below) to cycle through them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-help
A summary of all the possible options.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the SimpleJPEG library's version number (as major.minor.revision) and
exit.
.TP
.BI \-q " int
Specify the compression factor between 0 and 100. The default
is 75.
A small factor produces a smaller file with lower quality.
.TP
.B \-info
Overlay some file information on the display.
.TP
.BI \-alt " file
Specify an alternate picture file to compare against, toggled on and off by
holding the return key (see KEYS below).
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat the next argument as an input file name, even if it starts with a
dash.

.SH KEYS
The available key shortcuts are:
.IP
   'i' ............... overlay file information
.IP
   ' ' ............... show the original uncompressed picture
.IP
   up/down ........... change the compression factor by +/- 1 units
.IP
   left/right ........ change the compression factor by +/- 10 units
.IP
   return ............ show alternate picture (if specified with \-alt)
.IP
   0/1/2/3/4 ......... change the yuv_mode to
                        auto/yuv420/sharp-yuv420/yuv444/yuv400
.IP
   'o' ............... toggle Huffman optimization
.IP
   'a' ............... toggle adaptive quantization
.IP
   'b' ............... toggle adaptive bias
.IP
   'l' ............... toggle quantization limitation
.IP
   't' ............... toggle trellis-based quantization
.IP
   'e' ............... show error map
.IP
   'r' ............... show riskiness map
.IP
   'm' ............... print the source quantization matrices to the console
.IP
   '+'/'-' ........... go to next/previous file
.IP
   'h' ............... show this help message
.IP
   'q' / 'Q' / ESC ... quit

Just press 'h' for help.

